You're not getting away this time.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
You naughty laundry.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Hm?

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
I wonder what that is.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
It's awfully beautiful.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:43,020
Well, I can't go beyond

8
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:49,000
Oh my gosh.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,960
手間苦しいステージでその絡まった感動

10
00:00:56,960 --> 00:01:04,900
満足いくまで何回も壊してしまう

11
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:09,240
運命にとらえきさえ彷徨う明日は

12
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:15,720
雨の手を選んで何を手放しひとつになればいいんだよ

13
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:21,840
I love mycourse

14
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:25,600
dataset I家

15
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:32,900
but mulch

16
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:37,760
until this episode

17
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:41,620
sent me

18
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,720
but

19
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:52,020
You're scrunchie.

20
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:57,780
She still has it.

21
00:01:58,700 --> 00:01:59,880
You remember.

22
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:05,020
To tell you the truth, I've known for a while now.

23
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:08,460
Ever since our last battle.

24
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,760
He do it!

25
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:12,900
He do it!

26
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:15,880
Mama is here.

27
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,440
Hang on, He do it.

28
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:19,900
It hurt so much.

29
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:23,900
Like my heart was being torn into a thousand pieces.

30
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:28,340
But even through all that pain, I kept thinking,

31
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,700
I won't forget them.

32
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:32,900
He do it.

33
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,840
But I knew what it meant to lose you.

34
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,580
And I knew that pain would be even worse.

35
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,320
I won't be alone!

36
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,160
Welcome back!

37
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:45,960
But wait, if you remembered, then why didn't you tell us sooner?

38
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,680
Because I wanted my wish to come true.

39
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,820
Because I wanted to win.

40
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:53,600
The wish itself didn't matter.

41
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:58,680
If I won enough, Yuzuki would complete the oath again like she did with Hanayo.

42
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,180
And then she'd be freed from the card.

43
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:04,140
That's right, isn't it?

44
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:09,060
What are you saying, Ito-e?

45
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:10,600
That wouldn't solve anything!

46
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,040
You'd end up like me!

47
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:18,160
I'm flattered you care so much, but please don't worry about me.

48
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,680
I don't see this as a bad thing.

49
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:23,000
In fact, it's more like a dream come true.

50
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,880
Being with friends, making a noble sacrifice to save them.

51
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,060
It's all just so romantic.

52
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,600
I'm happy such a beautiful thing even exists.

53
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:46,640
Of course, the battles and stuff are incredible, but meeting the two of you, seeing what real friendship is like, to me, that's, I guess, it's like a miracle.

54
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:58,300
Finding a friend who can do something important for you, and being able to give something back to that friend?

55
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:03,440
If I have that, then there's not a single wish in the world I need.

56
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,280
Ito-e!

57
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,940
Doing something for a friend.

58
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:14,760
Please, Tama.

59
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,900
Will you finally listen to my wish?

60
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,360
Oh no.

61
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,900
We have to free Yuzuki from the card.

62
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:25,140
There's a chance to save my friends.

63
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,880
Nothing's more important than that.

64
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:37,460
I don't want you to be so sad.

65
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:41,380
If I help, will you be friends with me too?

66
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:41,860
Uh-huh.

67
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:45,160
Okay!

68
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:47,500
You tell Tama what to do.

69
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:50,960
Battling's about all I'm good for.

70
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:58,300
But if that can make your wish come true, battle and battle, as much as it takes.

71
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,880
Thank you, Tama.

72
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,480
All right, guys!

73
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,340
You ready?

74
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,660
Let's continue the match!

75
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:10,300
Oh, but Hito-e, one last thing.

76
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:13,520
I'm sorry, but there's no way I'll lose!

77
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:16,320
I've made my wish, and it's coming true!

78
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:17,480
Unko!

79
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:18,560
Attack!

80
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:19,020
Arc!

81
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:19,480
Aura!

82
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:34,920
Good game!

83
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:35,900
Good game.

84
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:42,680
I lost.

85
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,420
Hope that didn't hurt, Yuzuki.

86
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:48,280
Only my pride.

87
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,680
Oh, hey! What about your wish?

88
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:53,140
Oh, yeah! You finally figured it out?

89
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,480
It's clear now.

90
00:05:56,960 --> 00:06:00,960
I want Yuzuki and all the other girls trapped in cards to be free.

91
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,680
What? Ruko, that's...

92
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,380
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

93
00:06:03,380 --> 00:06:06,680
Slow down! We need to talk about this.

94
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,080
But we did.

95
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:10,980
You're the ones who made me realize what I needed to do.

96
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:14,420
If there's something I can do for my friends, I should do it.

97
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:18,300
Nothing would make me happier, and that's final!

98
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:24,680
I'd better be going.

99
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:29,300
Wait a sec! I'm coming with you!

100
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:31,120
Meaning we're coming.

101
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,700
Then, you're okay with my wish?

102
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:35,520
You're sure?

103
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:39,940
I guess so. Not like I could change your mind.

104
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:42,460
Just make sure you get your wish right, huh?

105
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,180
I mean, yeah, duh, I want to get out of this card.

106
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:48,580
But this'll all be for nothing if you end up as an L-Rig yourself.

107
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,760
We're getting dumplings on the way home, and I want you there.

108
00:06:51,760 --> 00:07:10,840
So, hey, I can't wait to go shopping with you, Tama.

109
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:12,120
You know, in person.

110
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:14,240
Can we eat dumplings?

111
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:17,920
I was thinking I'd buy you some scrunchies, so you can match the rest of us.

112
00:07:19,060 --> 00:07:20,060
Sounds great.

113
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:39,260
Oh, boy. Not good with heights.

114
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:43,700
I'd feel better about it if I could pick out my apartment.

115
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:49,700
Grandma.

116
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:57,240
I've been expecting you.

117
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:58,580
Hi, Ru.

118
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:00,100
Okay.

119
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,300
And you brought your little friends.

120
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,560
Yeah, what's it to you?

121
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,940
She is our friend, and we're here to support her.

122
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:07,600
Fine with me.

123
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:11,140
A cheering section won't make any difference.

124
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:13,320
Anything else, Ru?

125
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,560
A rousing speech, perhaps?

126
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:18,120
Or something you'd like to ask me?

127
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,800
No questions. No speeches.

128
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,520
All I want is to battle you.

129
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,560
You really are the best.

130
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:33,300
Open!

131
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:48,360
What a dark and lonely place.

132
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,360
Is it...

133
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:52,640
always so scary when you fight?

134
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:53,320
I'm sorry.

135
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:55,160
I thought you were all out of questions.

136
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:58,220
Ready when you are.

137
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:16,020
You're up first, Ru.

138
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:18,820
Tama, grow!

139
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:24,180
Grow.

140
00:09:24,180 --> 00:09:33,020
They're both so strong.

141
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:34,040
But look at Ruko.

142
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:35,200
I know.

143
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:36,460
Something's off.

144
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:37,860
Her eyes are so cold.

145
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:41,360
I don't get this.

146
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:46,020
Battles before were always fun or exciting or something.

147
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:47,900
This is just hollow.

148
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:48,540
Hollow.

149
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,360
It's so quiet.

150
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:02,340
I can even hear Tama breathing.

151
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,160
This may be my final battle.

152
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,140
I can't have any doubts.

153
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:10,880
Tama, grow!

154
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,620
Use sword ability!

155
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:29,200
Focus.

156
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:31,820
She's one of a kind.

157
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:33,040
Gotta give her that.

158
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:37,900
Of course, you have more than enough wins to have your wish granted.

159
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:40,480
It's just the time wasn't quite right.

160
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:43,220
This might give it the push you need, though.

161
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:45,360
Assuming you're ready, that is.

162
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:47,640
Not just yet.

163
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:48,680
Now grow.

164
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:51,000
Trust me.

165
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:52,760
It won't be much longer.

166
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:54,600
This isn't for my sake.

167
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:56,020
But for Ru's.

168
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:58,800
My dear Ruko Kominato.

169
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,120
Black desire!

170
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:04,500
Tama!

171
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:11,200
Tama.

172
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,040
What?

173
00:11:18,160 --> 00:11:18,760
Tama!

174
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:18,880
Tama!

175
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,000
Tama.

176
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:30,800
Can you hear me?

177
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:32,120
That's not Ru.

178
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:33,160
Tama.

179
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:35,500
But I know that voice.

180
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:38,200
Better than Ru's.

181
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:40,340
Maybe better than my own.

182
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:44,140
It must have been from a long time ago.

183
00:11:45,100 --> 00:11:46,720
You've finally come to see me.

184
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:48,980
Who...

185
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:50,380
Who are you?

186
00:11:58,380 --> 00:11:58,820
Oh...

187
00:11:58,820 --> 00:11:59,980
Hmm.

188
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:04,880
You poor thing.

189
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:07,380
All the pain she's put you through.

190
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:11,360
Ru is...

191
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,580
So cruel.

192
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:16,600
A wish to be together.

193
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:20,340
To never draw apart no matter what.

194
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:23,780
A dream that you believed in with all your heart.

195
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:27,660
I know you love Ru.

196
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:30,540
But she cares for her friends more than you.

197
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:31,800
No!

198
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,500
You got it all wrong!

199
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:36,040
Ru's not like that.

200
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:37,920
She said she'd be friends with me too.

201
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:38,640
Tama.

202
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:41,540
After this we were gonna go eat ice cream and dumplings.

203
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:45,980
And then I was gonna get a matching scrunchie so I could be like her other friends.

204
00:12:46,220 --> 00:12:47,340
I'm so sorry.

205
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:52,480
It's true that Ru loves her friends.

206
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:55,460
She loves them so much that she lied to you.

207
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:58,940
And now she's going to become an L-Rig for them.

208
00:12:58,980 --> 00:12:59,720
That's wrong!

209
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:02,280
We're all going home together after this.

210
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,880
So we have to win!

211
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,000
That won't happen.

212
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,140
Please listen to me.

213
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:07,920
Tama.

214
00:13:08,400 --> 00:13:09,320
Try to remember.

215
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:22,440
The solution is easy.

216
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:27,680
You want to stop Ru from becoming an L-Rig, don't you?

217
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:30,180
You don't have to lose the fight.

218
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,540
You can refuse the wish at the very end.

219
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:35,800
Yuzuki said the same thing, right?

220
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:40,400
For a selector's wish to be fulfilled, the L-Rig must be in agreement.

221
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:45,540
But then, what'll happen to Ru's wish?

222
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:47,420
Win the battle and see.

223
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:52,820
Then you'll know her true feelings, and you'll see why I'm trying to protect you.

224
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:54,900
Protect me?

225
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,060
But only if you win.

226
00:13:59,240 --> 00:13:59,720
Tama!

227
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:01,060
Tama!

228
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,560
Are you able to get back up?

229
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,580
I'll find out her true feelings.

230
00:14:08,920 --> 00:14:10,620
If you're still hurt, don't overdo it.

231
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:13,400
I'll fight, and I'll win the battle.

232
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:16,200
And then, it'll all be over.

233
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:17,640
Tama!

234
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:21,280
That's a good girl.

235
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:24,120
Hate to see you give up when it's just getting fun.

236
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,960
Drawing!

237
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,400
Enter charge!

238
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,920
Tama to level four!

239
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:34,660
No matter what happens after my wish, this is the last battle.

240
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:37,940
I don't know if it'll come true, or if everything will fall apart.

241
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,240
But we have to win!

242
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:41,300
This is the end!

243
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:45,720
What's that?

244
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:47,320
It's not an attack.

245
00:14:47,620 --> 00:14:48,300
What's happening?

246
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:52,000
The battlefield's coming apart!

247
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:57,120
The roof!

248
00:14:57,120 --> 00:15:14,080
Were we kicked out of the battlefield for some reason?

249
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:20,540
No, look. The sky. And it seems like they're still fighting.

250
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:32,840
Okay, Rue, what should I do for my next attack? Hurry!

251
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,860
It's so beautiful.

252
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:43,000
And I just noticed. You can see our apartment from here.

253
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:46,200
That does make me feel better.

254
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,920
Rue, what are you...

255
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:49,860
Thanks, Thalma.

256
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:54,360
You wanted me to see it one last time before the end, didn't you?

257
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,440
The end?

258
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,680
Bye, Grandma.

259
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:03,140
I love you.

260
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:10,640
Can you believe it, Iona? She thinks she's already won this.

261
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:11,940
She's the best.

262
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:14,860
She honestly is.

263
00:16:16,420 --> 00:16:17,360
My Rue.

264
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:19,900
What's the next step, Thalma?

265
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:26,560
Before the last attack, an oath.

266
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,520
Okay, I'm ready.

267
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:35,500
That's right. Before my wish was granted, I took a oath with Hanuyo, too.

268
00:16:36,460 --> 00:16:39,360
It seals the final contract between you and your L-Rate.

269
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:40,360
But wait!

270
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:43,440
If Thalma lost her memory, how does she know this?

271
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:55,160
Tell me what to say, and I'll say it.

272
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:00,600
Maybe she was lying to me.

273
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,540
She's not thinking about going back.

274
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:05,500
